**Project:** Greenteaguyz/NEXORA (Angular 18 Desktop Storefront)
**Topic:** Impeccable Theme Contrast & Light/Dark Mode Visibility Hardening

---

## What We Are Building

A comprehensive UI craft and theme contrast hardening pass across NEXORA.
The goal was eliminating invisible white-on-white text, dark navy flashes on hover over light cards, and un-themed dark elevation blocks in Light Mode while verifying Dark Mode stability and anti-slop design constraints (grounded hovers, zero raw emojis, and strict radii tokens).

---

## What WORKED (with evidence)

- **`impeccable-theme-contrast.spec.ts`** — confirmed by: 7/7 PASSED (100% automated test pass on all contrast and light-mode hover rules).
- **`impeccable-anti-slop.spec.ts`** — confirmed by: 7/7 PASSED (100% pass on anti-slop constraints, zero emojis, grounded hovers).
- **TypeScript Typecheck** — confirmed by: `tsc --noEmit --skipLibCheck` exited with code 0 (zero compilation errors).
- **Return URL Sanitization** — confirmed by: `return-url.util.ts` & `register.component.ts` correctly block open redirect loops and circular auth redirects.
- **Santa Loop Dual Review** — confirmed by: Both independent reviewers returned PASS (NICE).

---

## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **CommonJS execution of `@angular/compiler` in raw Node** — failed because: Angular 18 ships ESM-only bundles (`.mjs`). Solved by using standalone Node test runners (`impeccable-theme-contrast.spec.ts` and `impeccable-anti-slop.spec.ts`) that read and validate source AST/tokens without importing angular runtime via CJS `require()`.

---

## What Has NOT Been Tried Yet

- Playwright visual snapshot regression tests in headed browser mode (`npm run test:e2e`).

